**Finding: Compliant** — no redline proposed.

Section 1 of the agreement affirmatively disclaims exclusivity: "Nothing herein is intended nor shall be construed as creating an exclusive arrangement between Customer and Kubient. This Agreement will not restrict Customer offering Inventory via other agents or otherwise selling Inventory to any third parties." This meets the preferred playbook position (no exclusivity or sole-supplier obligation on AP), and in fact goes further by expressly preserving AP's right to use alternative agents and buyers.

Other "exclusive" hits are benign and do not restrict our procurement freedom:
- p0002 — non-exclusive license grant *to us* (favourable);
- p0064 — exclusive jurisdiction/venue (forum, not dealing);
- p0065 — each party's exclusive ownership of its own marks;
- p0072 — entire-agreement wording;
- p0073 — sole and exclusive benefit of the parties (no third-party beneficiaries).

Targeted searches for requirements-contract, preferred/sole supplier, non-compete and "Customer shall not" restrictions returned nothing, so there is no hidden exclusive-dealing covenant binding AP.
